module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraImageSurjective.Inputs
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraImageSurjective.Quasicoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FPAlgebraSheaf.Polynomial
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeDominating.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraJoin.Generated
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Global sections of a quasi-coherent algebra generate finite type subalgebras

Let `X` be a scheme and `A` a quasi-coherent sheaf of commutative `𝒪_X`-algebras. Every global
section of `A` lies in a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A`, with no hypothesis on `X`
whatever.

This is the *generation* half of the colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] — step 2 of the
Stacks proof of [Stacks, Tag 01PG], transported to algebras. The subalgebra is the image of the
polynomial algebra sheaf `𝒪_X[x]`, and the morphism out of it is produced through the
anti-equivalence between quasi-coherent algebra sheaves and schemes affine over `X`: a global
section of `A` is a global function on the relative spectrum of `A`, hence a morphism over `X`
from that relative spectrum into the affine line, and the polynomial algebra sheaf is the
pushed-forward structure sheaf of affine space.

## Main definitions

* `homOfGlobalSections`: the morphism of schemes over `X` from the relative spectrum of `A` to
  affine `n`-space determined by `n` global sections of `A`.
* `polynomialHom`: the induced morphism of algebra sheaves `𝒪_X[x_i] ⟶ A`.

## Main results

* `polynomialHom_app_top_coord`: `polynomialHom` sends the `i`-th coordinate of affine `n`-space,
  read as a global section of `𝒪_X[x_i]`, to the `i`-th given global section of `A`.
* `exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top`: **a global section of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf
  lies in a finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra**, unconditionally on `X`.

## What this does and does not do for Tag 05JT

The colimit assertion of [Stacks, Tag 05JT] is reduced by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections`
to the statement that for
**every affine open** `U` and every `x ∈ A(U)` some finite type quasi-coherent subalgebra of `A`
has a section over `U` mapping to `x`. What is proved here is exactly that statement at `U = ⊤`.
The remaining content is therefore the *extension* step, [Stacks, Tag 01PF]: a finite type
quasi-coherent subobject defined over a quasi-compact open of a quasi-compact quasi-separated
scheme is the restriction of a finite type quasi-coherent subobject of the whole scheme. **No
stacks attribute is attached below**: the colimit assertion is not proved, and nothing here
carries the quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of the tag, which is exactly where the
extension step needs them.

A section over an affine open `U` is *not* in general in the image of a subalgebra generated by
global sections, so the general case does not reduce to `U = ⊤` by shrinking `U`: on `ℙ¹` the
algebra `Sym(𝒪(-1))` has only the constants as global sections, while it is itself a finite type
quasi-coherent subalgebra of itself. That is why the extension step is irreducible rather than an
artifact of the reduction used here.

## Implementation notes

Affine space is given a **name** as an object over `X` rather than being written as
`Over.mk (𝔸(n; X) ↘ X)` inline, for the reason recorded in the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FiniteTypeDominating/Basic.lean`: written inline, `polynomialHom`
asks the unifier to identify `pushforwardAlgebra (Over.mk (𝔸(n; X) ↘ X)).hom` with
`pushforwardAlgebra (𝔸(n; X) ↘ X)`, and it unfolds `pushforwardAlgebra` on both sides and exceeds
the heartbeat limit. Indeed, that definition times out at `whnf` without the name and
elaborates in seconds with it.

The quasi-coherence of `A` is carried as an **instance** argument on the definitions rather than
as a hypothesis, because `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOver` takes it
that way; carrying it as a hypothesis would mean opening it with `letI` inside the *type* of
`homOfGlobalSections`, which makes that type a `let`-expression that tactics see through only with
`zetaDelta`.

The sections over `⊤` of `Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence.pushforwardAlgebraMap` are computed by
`Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence.pushforwardAlgebraMap_app`, which produces an
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE` between the preimages of `⊤`; those preimages are `⊤` by
`TopologicalSpace.Opens.map_top`, which is `rfl`, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app` closes the gap by `Eq.trans` at the elaborator's
transparency. It cannot be applied by `rw`: its pattern needs the source open to be literally
`f ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤`, and the goal has the equal-but-not-syntactic `(relativeSpecOver A).hom ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤`.
`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.homOfVector_appTop_coord` likewise has to be applied through
`congrArg` rather than `rw`, because `TopCat.Sheaf` is a `def` and so the goal is not
type-correct at the `implicit` transparency `rw` uses to build its motive — the error blames a
missing pattern that is character-for-character present.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open Stacks.RelativeSpec Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag05JTColimitGlobal

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **Affine `n`-space as an object over `X`.** The point of naming it is that every type below
then mentions `(affineSpaceOver X n).hom` rather than `𝔸(n; X) ↘ X`, so that the two spellings
have to be identified only once — see the implementation notes. -/
def affineSpaceOver (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : Type u) : Over X :=
  Over.mk (𝔸(n; X) ↘ X)

/-- The structure morphism of `affineSpaceOver X n` is the projection from affine space. -/
theorem affineSpaceOver_hom (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : Type u) :
    (affineSpaceOver X n).hom = 𝔸(n; X) ↘ X :=
  rfl

/-- The projection from affine space is an affine morphism. -/
instance isAffineHom_affineSpaceOver (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : Type u) :
    IsAffineHom (affineSpaceOver X n).hom :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsAffineHom (𝔸(n; X) ↘ X))

/-- The projection from affine `n`-space for `n` finite is locally of finite presentation. -/
instance locallyOfFinitePresentation_affineSpaceOver (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : Type u) [Finite n] :
    LocallyOfFinitePresentation (affineSpaceOver X n).hom :=
  inferInstanceAs (LocallyOfFinitePresentation (𝔸(n; X) ↘ X))

/-- The polynomial algebra sheaf is the pushed-forward structure sheaf of affine space, by
definition. -/
theorem polynomialAlgebra_eq (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : Type u) :
    Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.polynomialAlgebra X n = pushforwardAlgebra (affineSpaceOver X n).hom :=
  rfl

/-- **The polynomial algebra sheaf in finitely many variables is of finite type.** It is of finite
presentation by `Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.isOfFinitePresentation_pushforwardAlgebra`, since the
projection from affine space is affine and locally of finite presentation, and a finitely
presented ring map is of finite type. -/
theorem isFiniteType_affineSpacePushforward (X : Scheme.{u}) (n : Type u) [Finite n] :
    AlgebraSheaf.IsFiniteType (pushforwardAlgebra (affineSpaceOver X n).hom) := fun U hU =>
  RingHom.FiniteType.of_finitePresentation
    (Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.isOfFinitePresentation_pushforwardAlgebra
      (affineSpaceOver X n).hom U hU)

section

variable (A : AlgebraSheaf X) [AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A]

/-- **The morphism of schemes over `X` from the relative spectrum of `A` to affine `n`-space
determined by `n` global sections of `A`.** A global section of `A` is a global function on the
relative spectrum through
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.homOfVector` turns a family of those into a morphism over `X`. -/
@[ega "IV 17.11.3" "special case"]
def homOfGlobalSections (n : Type u) (v : n → A.right.obj.obj (op ⊤)) :
    FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOver A ⟶ affineSpaceOver X n :=
  Over.homMk
    (AffineSpace.homOfVector (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOver A).hom
      fun i => (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso A).inv.right.hom.app (op ⊤) (v i))
    (AffineSpace.homOfVector_over _ _)

/-- **The morphism of algebra sheaves `𝒪_X[x_i] ⟶ A` determined by `n` global sections of `A`.**
It is the pushforward of `homOfGlobalSections`, followed by the identification of the
pushed-forward structure sheaf of the relative spectrum with `A`. -/
def polynomialHom (n : Type u) (v : n → A.right.obj.obj (op ⊤)) :
    pushforwardAlgebra (affineSpaceOver X n).hom ⟶ A :=
  pushforwardAlgebraMap (homOfGlobalSections A n v) ≫
    (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso A).hom

/-- **`polynomialHom` sends the `i`-th coordinate to the `i`-th given global section.** The
sections over `⊤` of a pushed-forward morphism are its map on global functions, which on the
coordinates of affine `n`-space is
`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.homOfVector_appTop_coord`; the final identification cancels the
one used to define the vector. -/
theorem polynomialHom_app_top_coord (n : Type u) (v : n → A.right.obj.obj (op ⊤)) (i : n) :
    (polynomialHom A n v).right.hom.app (op ⊤) (AffineSpace.coord X i) = v i := by
  have hmap : (pushforwardAlgebraMap (homOfGlobalSections A n v)).right.hom.app (op ⊤) =
      (homOfGlobalSections A n v).left.appTop :=
    (pushforwardAlgebraMap_app (homOfGlobalSections A n v) (⊤ : X.Opens)
      (preimage_le_preimage_preimage _ _)).trans (Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app _)
  change (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso A).hom.right.hom.app (op ⊤)
      ((pushforwardAlgebraMap (homOfGlobalSections A n v)).right.hom.app (op ⊤)
        (AffineSpace.coord X i)) = v i
  rw [hmap]
  refine (congrArg
    (fun t => (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso A).hom.right.hom.app (op ⊤) t)
    (AffineSpace.homOfVector_appTop_coord (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOver A).hom
      (fun j => (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso A).inv.right.hom.app (op ⊤) (v j))
      i)).trans ?_
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
    (congrArg (fun f : A ⟶ A => f.right.hom.app (op ⊤))
      (FiniteTypeDominating.relativeSpecOverIso A).inv_hom_id) (v i)

end

/-- **A global section of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf lies in a finite type quasi-coherent
subalgebra of it.** The subalgebra is the image of the morphism out of the polynomial algebra
sheaf in one variable sending that variable to the section.

No hypothesis on `X` is used: not quasi-compactness, not quasi-separatedness, not affineness.
This is the affine-sections hypothesis of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteTypeSubalgebraFiltered.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections`
at the open `⊤`; the
hypothesis for a general affine open additionally needs the extension step
[Stacks, Tag 01PF], which is not proved here. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_top (A : AlgebraSheaf X)
    (hA : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent A) (x : A.right.obj.obj (op ⊤)) :
    ∃ (B : FiniteTypeSubalgebras.FiniteTypeSubalgebra A)
      (y : (B.obj : AlgebraSheaf X).right.obj.obj (op ⊤)),
        B.obj.arrow.right.hom.app (op ⊤) y = x := by
  have := hA
  have hCqc : AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent
      (pushforwardAlgebra (affineSpaceOver X PUnit.{u + 1}).hom) :=
    isQuasicoherent_pushforwardAlgebra _
  have hCft := isFiniteType_affineSpacePushforward X PUnit.{u + 1}
  refine FiniteTypeSubalgebras.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_section_of_factorisation
    (image.ι (polynomialHom A PUnit.{u + 1} fun _ => x))
    (factorThruImage (polynomialHom A PUnit.{u + 1} fun _ => x))
    (Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsQuasicoherent X _ _ _ hCqc hA) hCqc hCft
    (Stacks.AlgebraImageSurjective.imageIsLocallySurjective X _ _ _)
    ⊤ x (AffineSpace.coord X PUnit.unit) ?_
  rw [image.fac]
  exact polynomialHom_app_top_coord A PUnit.{u + 1} (fun _ => x) PUnit.unit

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag05JTColimitGlobal

end
